From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:12:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] AyInstance::rewind: restart the chips

rewind only went back to the first op: the chips kept their registers,
counters and envelopes, and the player's buffer its samples, so a looped
voice did not start the dump again, and a seek back (a rewind, then
samples discarded) was offset by the stale samples. rewind now starts a
new player, as a new voice has.
---
 src/audiosource/ay/soloud_ay.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/ay/soloud_ay.cpp b/src/audiosource/ay/soloud_ay.cpp
index 92a56b6..6bc8ea1 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/ay/soloud_ay.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/ay/soloud_ay.cpp
@@ -61,6 +61,9 @@ namespace SoLoud
 
 	result AyInstance::rewind()
 	{
+		// Start the chips and their buffer again, as a new voice does.
+		delete mChip;
+		mChip = new ChipPlayer(this);
 		mPos = 0;
 		return SO_NO_ERROR;
 	}
